\cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095  \cf8 is there any way we can leverage the variables for seo title or dont worry?\cf5                                                                                                     \cb3 \
\
\cf8 \uc0\u9210 \cf5  Yes, worth using them. Yoast has variables you can insert into the SEO title field rather than typing static text. The most useful ones for category pages are:\
\
  - 
\f1\b \cf6 %%term_title%%
\f0\b0 \cf5  \'97 inserts the category name automatically\
  - 
\f1\b \cf6 %%sitename%%
\f0\b0 \cf5  \'97 inserts "Bruce McKenzie Booksellers" automatically\
\
  So instead of typing \cf11 Biography\cf5  \cf11 &\cf5  \cf11 Memoir\cf5  \cf11 Books\cf5  \cf11 |\cf5  \cf11 Bruce\cf5  \cf11 McKenzie\cf5  \cf11 Booksellers\cf5  manually for every category, you could set the 
\f1\b \cf6 global
\f0\b0 \cf5  
\f1\b \cf6 default
\f0\b0 \cf5  in Yoast to:\
\
  \cf12 \uc0\u9614 \cf5  
\f3\i\b \cf13 %%term_title%%
\f0\i0\b0 \cf5  
\f3\i\b \cf13 |
\f0\i0\b0 \cf5  
\f3\i\b \cf13 %%sitename%%
\f0\i0\b0 \cf5 \
\
  This would automatically generate titles like:\
  - \cf11 Biographies\cf5  \cf11 |\cf5  \cf11 Bruce\cf5  \cf11 McKenzie\cf5  \cf11 Booksellers\cf5 \
  - \cf11 Fiction\cf5  \cf11 |\cf5  \cf11 Bruce\cf5  \cf11 McKenzie\cf5  \cf11 Booksellers\cf5 \
  - \cf11 Children\cf5  \cf11 |\cf5  \cf11 Bruce\cf5  \cf11 McKenzie\cf5  \cf11 Booksellers\cf5 \
\
  The downside is it uses the exact category name, so \cf11 Biographies\cf5  rather than the more descriptive \cf11 Biography\cf5  \cf11 &\cf5  \cf11 Memoir\cf5  \cf11 Books\cf5 . For most categories that's fine, but for a few (like\
   \cf11 Well\cf5  \cf11 Being\cf5  or \cf11 Sciences\cf5 ) a custom title would rank better.\
\
  
\f1\b \cf6 My
\f0\b0 \cf5  
\f1\b \cf6 recommendation:
\f0\b0 \cf5 \
  - Set the global default to \cf11 %%term_title%%\cf5  \cf11 |\cf5  \cf11 %%sitename%%\cf5  \'97 this covers all categories instantly\
  - Then manually override the SEO title only for categories where the name isn't descriptive enough\
\
