\cf9 \cb10 \uc0\u10095  \cf8 perfect can we do the same for meta description and use variable\cf5                                                                                                                \cb3 \
\
\cf8 \uc0\u9210 \cf5  Unfortunately Yoast doesn't have a useful variable for meta descriptions on category pages \'97 there's no %%category_description%% variable that pulls the description you write.\
\
  The only variables available for meta descriptions are things like %%sitename%%, %%sep%%, %%term_title%% \'97 which aren't enough to build a meaningful meta description on their\
  own.\
\
  So meta descriptions need to be written manually for each category. However \'97 good news \'97 the meta description is less critical than the focus keyphrase and description. If\
  you leave it blank, Google will usually pull a relevant snippet from the category description you've written anyway.\
\
  
